    print-line-uni : Text -> [Console.Write] Nothing
    read-line  : [Console.Read] Text

Page 1

Chapter: RocAliasIndependent
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_closure_recursion_tests.zig,
 "inspect: list alias multiple independent lists", case 13 in file order:

     { x = [1, 2] _y = [3, 4] match x { [a, b] => a + b, _ => 0 } }

 and Roc expects 3.

 THE CONTROL FOR FINDING 60, and it is why this one is worth porting rather
 than skipping as a near-duplicate of case 10. Both have a binding nobody
 reads. In case 10 that binding's value is a BARE NAME, and the emitter's
 discard of it (`_ = x;`) is what zig refuses as a pointless discard of a local
 constant. Here the value is a LIST LITERAL, so the discard is of a call
 result, which zig accepts. The pair says the defect is about what is being
 discarded and not about unused bindings in general.

 Adaptations, standing: no list patterns, so `list-at`; Roc's `3.0` is `3`;
 Roc's `_y` discard sigil has no Codex spelling, so the binding is named and
 simply not read.

Section: Functions

  independent : Integer -> Integer
  independent (n) =
   let x = [1, 2]
   in let y = [3, 4]
   in list-at x 0 + list-at x 1

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show (independent 0))
  end
